{{#each results}}
The organisation measures whether its security measures work, and the management uses the results to improve them.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when NIS2 applies, or when the organisation runs an ISMS. NIS2 requires policies and procedures to assess the effectiveness of the cybersecurity risk-management measures.

== How to implement

Choose three to five metrics that show whether the most important measures work. Set a target for each metric. Measure them at least once a year, before the management review. For example:

* the share of the internal controls of this home with the assessment "OK", from the section "Status" of the home card
* the share of the critical updates that were installed within the deadline
* the share of the user accounts with multi-factor authentication
* the share of the people who completed the security training
* the time from the detection of a significant incident to the first notification.

